Package: enfs-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 dkms (>= 2.8),
 build-essential,
 linux-headers-generic | linux-headers
Recommends: nfs-common
Description: Enhanced NFS multipath client (DKMS source) for Ubuntu 24.04 / 26.04
 enfs is the OpenEuler "Enhanced NFS" client, providing multipath mounts,
 round-robin RPC dispatch and transport failover on top of the in-tree
 Linux NFS client.
 .
 This package ships the source under /usr/src/enfs-<ver>/ and registers
 it with DKMS, which builds replacement sunrpc.ko, nfs.ko, nfsv3.ko,
 lockd.ko, nfs_acl.ko and the new enfs.ko on package install and on
 every kernel upgrade. The replacement modules are placed in
 /lib/modules/$(uname -r)/updates/ and take precedence over the in-tree
 Ubuntu modules.
 .
 The package is `Architecture: all` because it ships only source —
 DKMS performs the per-kernel arch-specific compile on the user's
 machine. One .deb works on both amd64 and arm64.
 .
 Removing this package via "apt purge enfs-dkms" restores the stock
 Ubuntu modules and rebuilds the initramfs accordingly.
